[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62888,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Solitary fibrous tumour (SFT) is a neoplasm with fibroblastic differentiation, with prominent, branching, thin-walled vessels and <em>NAB2</em>-<em>STAT6</em> gene rearrangement.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62889,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8815/1 Solitary fibrous tumour NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62890,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F74 &amp; XH7E62 Neoplasms of uncertain behaviour of peritoneum &amp; Solitary fibrous tumour NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62891,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> haemangiopericytoma; giant cell angiofibroma; benign solitary fibrous tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62892,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fat-forming (lipomatous) solitary fibrous tumour; giant cell&ndash;rich solitary fibrous tumour; dedifferentiated solitary fibrous tumour; solitary fibrous tumour, malignant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62893,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Peritoneum, omentum, mesentery, retroperitoneum, and abdominal wall {17006407; 25753542; 24394146; 30957324; 12076279}</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62894,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SFT usually presents with signs and symptoms related to an abdominal mass; it is often associated with pain and occasionally with hypoglycaemia {29660566; 23302323; 25731568; 25753542}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62895,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SFT is an uncommon tumour seen over a wide age range, with peak incidence in the fifth and sixth decades of life {29660566}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62896,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62897,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is a <em>NAB2</em> and <em>STAT6</em> gene fusion due to paracentric inversion on chromosome&nbsp;12q {23313954; 23761323; 23313952}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62898,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SFT tends to be circumscribed, solid, and variably sized {29660566; 30957324; 17006407}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62899,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This tumour is composed of spindled to ovoid cells with indistinct, eosinophilic cytoplasm growing in a patternless fashion within a variably collagenous stroma. There are branching, thin-walled staghorn blood vessels, which may be hyalinized. Myxoid change may be present. Tumours usually show a low mitotic count and no significant nuclear pleomorphism or necrosis, although cellularity may be high. Rare tumours may contain mature adipose tissue (fat-forming), an admixed population of multinucleated giant cells (giant cell), or transition to sarcoma (dedifferentiated). SFT is typically positive for CD34 and STAT6, but expression can be lost in dedifferentiated cases {29660566}. STAT6 immunohistochemistry is a sensitive and specific surrogate for all fusions seen in these tumours {24030747; 24702701; 23575898}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62900,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cytology material shows oval, elongated, or rounded cells with wispy cytoplasm and eosinophilic collagenous stroma {28914981}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62901,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>NAB2</em>-<em>STAT6</em> gene fusions are pathognomonic for SFT, but the detection of fusion types is difficult without multiplexed sequencing assays.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62902,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> spindled/oval-shaped cells; branching thin vessels; variable collagen deposition; CD34 and/or STAT6 expression (where available).</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable (in selected cases):</em> demonstration of <em>NAB2</em>-<em>STAT6</em> gene fusion.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62903,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Risk stratification models are preferred over anatomical staging {22575866}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:17:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62904,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "<p>Across all sites of involvement, the recurrence rate is about 30% {22575866; 29039030; 28838212; 26924782; 30206022}, and as high as 40% after 5&nbsp;years {1203874; 9850176}; recurrence has rarely occurred after 15&nbsp;years {29039030}. The most widely used multivariate model for metastatic risk incorporates mitotic count (&gt;&nbsp;2&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup>, equating to &ge;&nbsp;4&nbsp;mitoses/10&nbsp;HPF of 0.55&nbsp;mm in diameter and 0.24&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> in area), patient age (&ge;&nbsp;55&nbsp;years), and tumour size stratified by 5&nbsp;cm tiers to classify tumours into low-risk, intermediate-risk, and high-risk groups {22575866}. Adding necrosis as a variable results in a higher number of cases being classified as low-risk {28731041; 29935303}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-19T16:04:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]